# PAM stack for the WriteOnce greeter (writeonce-greeter). Mirror of
# /etc/pam.d/login: pam_unix for auth/account/session, plus pam_systemd
# (session) so logind registers the session — XDG_RUNTIME_DIR, seat0, VT —
# which the chosen Wayland compositor needs to take DRM master. pam_systemd is
# `optional` so a logind hiccup never blocks login (you can still pick the
# Shell session and debug). The service name MUST match greeter.toml's
# `pam-service` — a mismatch makes PAM fall back to `other` (deny) = lockout.
auth      required   pam_unix.so
account   required   pam_unix.so
session   required   pam_unix.so
session   optional   pam_systemd.so
